Connection Methods
1. Via Huawei-Guest WiFi (In-Office)
When physically at HKRC and connected to the Huawei-Guest WiFi network, you can directly connect to the servers using their Public IP addresses without any additional proxy configuration.

2. Via XGate Proxy (Remote / Standard Corporate Network)
By default, blue zone servers are only accessible via their public IPs over the Huawei-Guest WiFi network inside HKRC. However, arrangements have been made with the IT & Network department to allow access via XGate using an HTTP proxy.

Proxy Address: Hkgpqwg00206.huawei.com:8080
Authentication: Requires your Huawei ID and password.
Client Configuration
MobaXTerm (Recommended): This is the easiest method, as you only need to add the HTTP proxy details directly into your session network configuration.
IDEs (VSCode / Cursor): To route your IDE connection through the proxy, you must use ncat to pipe the connection.
Add the following snippet to your local ~/.ssh/config file:

Host toronto
    HostName 119.8.241.51
    User <username_on_toronto>
    Port 22
    ProxyCommand ncat --proxy Hkgpqwg00206.huawei.com:8080 --proxy-type http --proxy-auth <huawei-id>:<huawei-password> %h %p

Host fremont
    HostName 119.8.241.51
    User <username_on_fremont>
    Port 3005
    ProxyCommand ncat --proxy Hkgpqwg00206.huawei.com:8080 --proxy-type http --proxy-auth <huawei-id>:<huawei-password> %h %p
​
⚠️ Windows Users: Windows does not ship with ncat by default. You can download and install a suitable distribution from the Official Nmap Website.

3. Via WireGuard VPN (Work From Home / AI Tools)
For standard Work-From-Home (WFH) scenarios, you can use your Huawei-provided green zone laptop with the XGate HTTP proxy setup described above.

However, for special AI tool workflows that require direct backend access, we have established a dedicated WireGuard VPN to connect to the HK Compiler Lab blue zone environment.

VPN Server (Host): Hosted on the server fremont, exposed at 119.8.241.51:3008.
Account Requirement: You do not need a local user account on the server to use the VPN.
How to Connect
Request a WireGuard .conf configuration file from the lab administrator.
Import the .conf file into your local WireGuard client. If you find it difficult to transfer a config file, you may convert it to a QR code with this tool.
Activate the connection. This grants your machine direct access to the local 10.11.12.0/24 subnet, allowing you to reach both fremont and toronto via their WireGuard IPs.
⚠️ Windows/macOS Users: Windows & macOS do not ship with built-in WireGuard support. You can download and install a suitable client from the Official WireGuard Website.

