Operating System Policy
We have different policies for which OS is installed on each of our servers due to the differences in their target workload, as well as hardware architecture.

Toronto
Ice Lake is an old architecture, so we will default to a supported Ubuntu LTS for stability.

Fremont
Shimada Peak series Threadripper requires Linux kernel > 6.14 for CPU workload scheduling stability. Furthermore, due to our renewed focus on the open-source ecosystem, it is important that we have a base environment that keeps pace with upstream LLVM development. Hence, the choice of Fedora for this server.

Compatibility Issues
Users of the fremont server and less frequently the toronto server, will at times run into compatibility issues due to glibc, libstdc++, or ABI incompatibility issues with either the projects they are building, their dependent libraries, or the available featureset of the target hardware the compiled binaries will run on; sometimes, even all three.

We have thought of this problem as well and hence, support two different methods of cross-compilation:

Containers
